Description
Return a copy of `arg`. The value must have one of these types:
   - array
   - buffer (if compiled into driver)
   - class
   - mapping

   For example:
   int *a, *b = ({ 1 });
   a = b;
   a[0] = 2;
   printf("%O %O\n", a, b);

   The result is: ({ 2 }) ({ 2 })

   int *a, *b = ({ 1 });
   a = copy(b);
   a[0] = 2;
   printf("%O %O\n", a, b);

   The result is: ({ 2 }) ({ 1 })
